# tests/log — MIT #3 concurrent logging (week 9)

Stub created week 2 (design gate). Log header format frozen in docs/design.md §7.1.

## Planned tests

- `lg-nwriters`: N threads (1, 2, 4, 8) each create+write+unlink files concurrently;
  per-N throughput recorded and compared against stock-log baseline
  (bench/baseline.txt create = 1.6 ms/txn @ CPUS=1).
- `lg-crash-before`: kill QEMU mid-commit (before install) → reboot → FS consistent,
  no committed-op visibility.
- `lg-crash-after`: kill QEMU just after install → reboot → committed ops visible,
  FS consistent (recovery replay of loghdr txseq).
- `lg-assert`: run with `log_assert` invariants enabled (outstanding credits zero at
  commit end, no dirty blocks outside tx) across all other tests.

## Pass criteria

Concurrent writers ≥ stock-log throughput at N=4 (scaling documented); both crash
tests recover cleanly via scripted reboot check; zero assert trips in a full suite
run at CPUS=2.
